      "bounding box" : [ 52.158, 628.154, 492.688, 662.682 ],
      "font" : "SFBX1095",
      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "Lemma 6. Let Pnσ be a signed path of order n, then p+(Pnσ) = ⌊n2⌋. Yu et al. [4, Theorem 3.1] characterized all connected signed graph Gσ with p+(Gσ) = 1.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 52.157, 592.486, 548.218, 621.103 ],
      "font" : "SFBX1095",
      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "Lemma 7. Let Gσ be a connected signed graph. Then p+(Gσ) = 1 if and only if Gσ is a balanced complete multipartite signed graph.",
      "kids" : [ {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 2,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 52.157, 541.914, 548.22, 585.489 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "The length of a signed path (or simply a path) Pσ refers to the total number of edges in Pσ. For any two vertices y and z, the distance between them, denoted by d(y,z), is defined as the length of the shortest path between y and z."
      } ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 52.157, 499.264, 548.221, 534.863 ],
      "font" : "SFBX1095",
      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "Lemma 8. Let Gσ be a connected signed graph with girth gr and let Cσ be a shortest cycle in Gσ. If y,y′ ∈ V (Cσ) and there exists a path Pσ of length k from y to y′ satisfying (V (Pσ)\\{y,y′})∩V (Cσ) = ∅,",
      "kids" : [ {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 3,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 52.157, 491.342, 72.35, 505.055 ],
        "font" : "SFTI1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "then"
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 4,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 283.511, 469.456, 323.826, 495.491 ],
        "font" : "CMMI10",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "gr 2 ≤ k."
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 6,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 52.157, 409.0, 548.224, 467.48 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "Proof. Remember that Cσ have two different paths from y to y′. The total length of both the paths equals the length of Cσ, i.e., gr. Thus, the shorter length of these paths is at most g2 . The shorter of these two paths from y to y′, followed by the path Pσ, forms a cycle of length at most g2r + k. Therefore, we obtain:"
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 9,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 271.965, 387.377, 280.99, 413.149 ],
        "font" : "CMR10",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "gr 2"
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 11,
        "level" : "2",
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 52.158, 373.492, 335.367, 406.042 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "+ k ≥ gr, and consequently"
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 12,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 283.511, 351.605, 323.826, 377.641 ],
        "font" : "CMMI10",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "gr 2 ≤ k."
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 14,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 52.157, 337.983, 172.216, 351.75 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "This concludes the proof."
      }, {
        "type" : "table",
        "pdfua_tag" : "Table",
        "id" : 15,
        "level" : "3",
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 540.35, 341.474, 547.655, 348.796 ],
        "number of rows" : 1,
