      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 16,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 52.157, 284.926, 548.225, 328.501 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "Let Gσ[Hσ] be a subgraph of Gσ induced by Hσ, and let x be a vertex outside Hσ. We denote the distance between x and Gσ[Hσ] as: d(x,Gσ[Hσ]) = min{d(x,y) | y ∈ Hσ}. Next, we define Nj(Gσ[Hσ]) as:"
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 17,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 52.158, 243.524, 467.198, 283.995 ],
        "font" : "CMMI10",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "Nj(Gσ[Hσ]) = {x ∈ V (Gσ) \\ Hσ | d(x,Gσ[Hσ]) = j, j = 1,2,...,n}. The number of vertices in Nj(Gσ[Hσ]) is denoted by |Nj(Gσ[Hσ])|."
      } ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 52.158, 207.856, 548.217, 243.455 ],
      "font" : "SFBX1095",
      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "Lemma 9. Let Gσ be a connected signed graph with girth gr, and let Cσ be a shortest cycle in Gσ. If p+(Cσ) = p+(Gσ), then Nj(Cσ) = ∅ for j ≥ 2.",
      "kids" : [ {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 18,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 52.157, 164.266, 548.222, 207.842 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "Proof. Indeed, we only need to establish that N2(Cσ) = ∅. Suppose, for the sake of contradiction, that N2(Cσ) ̸= ∅. Let y′ ∈ N2(Cσ) and y′ ∼ y ∈ N1(Cσ). Then, y′ is a pendant vertex of Gσ[V (Cσ) ∪ {y,y′}]. Consequently,"
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 19,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 157.101, 142.38, 443.278, 163.566 ],
        "font" : "CMMI10",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "p+(Gσ) ≥ p+(Gσ[V (Cσ) ∪ {y,y′}]) = p+(Cσ) + 1 > p+(Cσ),"
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 20,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 52.158, 107.96, 548.217, 143.613 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "by Lemmas 1 and 2, which contradicts the assumption that p+(Cσ) = p+(Gσ). Hence, N2(Cσ) = ∅, and therefore, Nj(Cσ) = ∅ for j ≥ 3. This completes the proof."
      }, {
        "type" : "table",
